00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.179 align:start position:0%
360 degrees is one complete rotation and  you might think it's the same as 720  degrees or two complete rotations but  nature actually does distinguish between  the two  there are objects that are the same  after two rotations that are the same  after one these are called spinous and  the palm of your hand is one example  after one 360 degree rotation it isn't  the same but after a second lap or 720  degrees it returns to normal  a similar illustration can be done with  a belt or a long braid one end is fixed  and one can move I have a ribbon on the  back side to tell front and back apart  after one full spin there is no way to  untangle the hair without further  rotation but after another full spin 720  degrees there is now a way to return it  to how it was without rotating either  end just moving it up and across this  animation also shows the concept but  this time with mini belts and because  each belt is the same after two full  rotations the ends can spin continuously  without any becoming tangled
 

